@startuml
title Reschedule appointment

actor Client
participant "NGINX" as NGINX
participant "FE (Next.js)" as FE
participant "BE (Django/DRF)" as BE
database "DB (PostgreSQL)" as DB

Client -> FE : pick a new time
FE -> NGINX : POST /v1/appointments/{id}/reschedule  (X-CSRFToken)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  AuthN: session; AuthZ: role = client (ownership checked)
  appointments.views.AppointmentRescheduleView
  body: { new_start_at }
end note
BE -> BE : appointments.services.reschedule_appointment(by_client=true)
note over BE
  Business rules:
  - appointment must be status=booked
  - self-service blocked within 24h of current start_at
  - keeps snapshot duration; new end_at = new_start_at + duration
  - new_start_at: future, >= minimum_notice, <= horizon
  - lock staff row (select_for_update)
  - within schedule, no break/time-off, no overlap (excluding self)
  - UPDATE in place; status STAYS booked (never a cancellation)
end note
BE -> DB : SELECT ... FOR UPDATE (staff row)
BE -> DB : UPDATE appointment (start_at, end_at)
BE -> BE : notifications.notify_waitlist_for_freed_time()  ' old time freed
BE --> FE : 200 (AppointmentSerializer)
FE --> Client : new time confirmed
@enduml
